Adapted components, through the TypeScript:

1. types.go and phonetics.go
   Adapted from AttributesHelper.java, SurfaceTransition.java, SuffixTransition.java, and Zemberek's root and
   phonetic attribute definitions (RootAttribute, PhoneticAttribute). Root and phonetic attributes are 32-bit
   bit masks; Zemberek's suffix template notation (A, I, +x, >x, ~x, !x) is kept.

2. morphotactics.go
   Adapted from TurkishMorphotactics.java and Conditions.java: the Turkish finite-state morphotactics of nouns,
   compounds (CompoundP3sg), su/akarsu, adjectives, numerals, nominal predicates (ek-fiil and değil), pronouns,
   adverbs, postpositives, verbs (tenses, compound tenses, negation, ability, voice, verbal nouns, participles,
   converbs, the irregular demek/yemek), standalone question particles, and imek. Modified for the precision of
   formal spell checking: the colloquial vowel-dropped locative and ablative contractions
   (connectLastVowelDropWords: burda, içerde, ilerde...) are left out, the nominalization of closed-class
   function adjectives (nasıl, öyle, her...) and the locative of "daha" are restricted, pronominal -ki routes its
   cases through pronAfterRel_S to reject forms without the buffer consonant (*evdekiyi), and the productive -daş
   (>dAş) derivation is added.

3. dictionary.go and binary.go
   Adapted from StemTransitionsBase.java and Zemberek's .dict lexicon format (master-dictionary.dict,
   non-tdk.dict, informal.dict, proper.dict): .dict parsing, the inference of Turkish root attributes
   (Aorist_A/Aorist_I, Passive_In, Causative_t, ProgressiveVowelDrop, the voicing of non-verbs), the dummy
   CompoundP3sgRoot stems, and the special root alternations (ben/ban, sen/san, de/di, ye/yi, birbiri/birbir,
   çoğu/çok). The [A:Ext] and [A:Informal] entries and a few non-TDK entries of master-dictionary.dict are left
   out so that common misspellings are not accepted.

4. analyzer.go
   Adapted from RuleBasedAnalyzer.java, SearchPath.java and StemTransitionsMapBased.java, redesigned as a
   low-allocation forward search (offsets instead of substrings, linked path nodes, 64-entry per-transition
   surface caches, circumflex verification, a bounded result cache).

prior.go, fuzzy.go and morph.go are tinyfix-tr's own (the generative prior, the error-tolerant search and the
entry point) and use the adapted components above.


